1%AB%E8%87%B3%E3%82%8A%E3%81%BE%E3%81%97%E3%81%9F%E3%80%82%20%E5%BA%97%E8%88%97%E9%95%B7%E6%9C%9F%E4%BC%91%E6%A5%AD%E3%81%8A%E3%82%88%E3%81%B3%E8%8F%93%E5%AD%90%E8%A3%BD%E9%80%A0%E8%B2%A9%E5%A3%B2%E7%B5%82%E4%BA%86%E3%81%A8%E3%81%AA%E3%82%8A%E3%81%BE%E3%81%99%E3%81%8C%E3%80%81%E3%81%93%E3%82%8C%E3%81%BE%E3%81%A7%E7%9A%86%E6%A7%98%E3%81%AB%E3%81%94%E6%84%9B%E9%A1%A7%E3%81%84%E3%81%9F%E3%81%A0%E3%81%8D%E3%81%BE%E3%81%97%E3%81%9F%E6%9C%AC%E5%AE%B6%E5%B0%BE%E5%BC%B5%E5%B1%8B%E3%81%AE%E5%91%B3%E3%82%92%E3%80%81%E4%BD%95%E3%81%A8%E3%81%8B%E3%81%93%E3%82%8C%E3%81%8B%E3%82%89%E3%82%82%E5%B1%8A%E3%81%91%E7%B6%9A%E3%81%91%E3%82%8B%E6%96%B9%E6%B3%95%E3%81%AF%E3%81%AA%E3%81%84%E3%81%8B%E3%80%81%E3%81%82%E3%82%89%E3%82%86%E3%82%8B%E5%8F%AF%E8%83%BD%E6%80%A7%E3%82%92%E8%A6%96%E9%87%8E%E3%81%AB%E5%85%A5%E3%82%8C%E6%A4%9C%E8%A8%8E%E3%82%92%E9%87%8D%E3%81%AD%E3%81%A6%E3%81%8A%E3%82%8A%E3%81%BE%E3%81%99%E3%80%82]\nHonke Owariya has been associated with several temples in Kyoto from the Edo Period. It fostered bonds with Zen Buddhist sects from Kennin-ji, Shokoku-ji and Myoshin-ji.\nThe current and sixteenth owner of Honke Owariya is Ariko Inaoka, who follows in the tradition of her father (the 15th owner) and grandfather (the 14th owner).\nSee also\n*List of oldest companies\nReferences\nExternal links\n*[http://honke-owariya.co.jp/en Official website of Honke Owariya]\n*[https://www.google.sk/maps/place/Honke+Owariya/@35.0081998,135.7593137,16z/data=!4m8!1m2!2m1!1sowariya+kyoto!3m4!1s0x600108866944eae5:0xe30827bc558104bc!8m2!3d35.0127922!4d135.7601213 Location on Google Maps]"
